
Turn any invoice layout into the same eight clean JSON fields — and never invent a number that isn't on the page.

THE PROBLEM IT SOLVES
Every vendor formats invoices differently; finance teams re-key them by hand.
Downstream systems need identical JSON every time, whatever the layout.
A wrong total is worse than a blank one — silent errors flow everywhere.

WHAT THE CANDIDATE LEARNS
Zero-shot vs few-shot prompting
Role / system prompts, XML-tag structuring
Chain-of-thought reasoning
Forcing strictly valid JSON output
Prompt chaining: extract → verify → format
Temperature, max_tokens, stop sequences
Prompt versioning and A/B iteration

MUST BE IMPLEMENTED
15–20 self-made invoices — layouts varied, some fields left blank
A self-verify pass that re-checks the model's own extraction
In-prompt normalisation: dates to ISO, currency cleaned
Versioned prompt library v1→v5 with accuracy measured per version
